From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yuwei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:36:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Share a layout's shaped text

What an embedder keeps of a layout (a line's glyph runs) copied their
glyphs out of it, walking parley's iterators each time the lines were
broken. Layout::shaped_text now gives the layout's ShapedText
(re-exported) as an Arc, so what is kept of a layout can hold it and
walk the glyphs later, as Blink's ShapeResultView does.

It is never changed under whoever holds it: rebuilding the layout takes
a new one where the old one is held (LayoutData::clear), and breaking
the lines copies it before changing a tab's advance where it is held
(Arc::make_mut). The kept shapings share it with their layouts instead
of copying it, and a layout that takes one copies it only when its
characters are styled otherwise.

GlyphRun::span (GlyphSpan) gives where a glyph run's glyphs are in the
shaped text (its shaped run and clusters), its direction and its line's
spacing (EffectiveSpacing, now PartialEq); GlyphSpan::glyphs walks them
from the shaped text alone, through the Glyphs iterator that
GlyphRun::glyphs uses.
